                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-07-30T23:48:00.972075858Z
                                author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                                kind @note
                                text "TraversalMark (src/build.rs:144-158) is a magic-sentinel newtype: struct TraversalMark(usize) with const UNMARKED = Self(usize::MAX), where is_marked_for(edge) compares self.0 against edge.index() and mark(edge) stores it. It records which traversal root last marked an edge, so the value is either an edge identifier or nothing — precisely Option<EdgeId>. The arena_id! documentation at src/util.rs:20-25 already advertises that the niche-packed NonZeroU32 makes Option<Id> four bytes rather than sixteen, and every other side table in the codebase takes that route; dependency_marks is the one place that did not get the message. Converting halves Plan::dependency_marks from Vec<usize> to Vec<Option<EdgeId>> (32 KiB to 16 KiB on a 4,000-edge graph, with correspondingly better locality in rebuild_frontier, which fills and rescans it), turns is_marked_for into self.0 == Some(edge), and makes an unmarked slot stop being representable as a valid edge index. Note that rebuild_frontier resets the table with fill(TraversalMark::UNMARKED) on every call, so the reset becomes fill(None). Deliberately no percentage estimated; do it for the type safety and treat any speed as incidental."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-07-30T23:52:45.714258388Z
                                author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-07-30T23:54:26.991418749Z
                                author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                                kind @decision
                                text "Done. TraversalMark — a repr(transparent) newtype over usize with usize::MAX standing for \"unmarked\" — is deleted, and dependency_marks becomes Vec<Option<EdgeId>>. is_marked_for(edge) becomes a comparison against Some(edge), mark(edge) an assignment of Some(edge), and both the resize in synchronize_arenas and the reset in rebuild_frontier now pass None. The niche in the NonZeroU32 identifier makes the empty case free, so the table halves from eight bytes per edge to four — 32 KiB to 16 KiB on a 4,000-edge graph — and an unmarked slot stops being representable as a valid edge index. Measured: wide no-op 22,776,535 to 22,744,529 instructions, −0.14%; command evaluation unchanged at 40,892,549, which is expected because that fixture runs the commands tool and never reaches rebuild_frontier. This node deliberately carried no estimate, and the outcome matches the stated reason for doing it — the type safety is the point and the 0.14% is incidental. It also removes the last magic-value sentinel standing against the arena_id! documentation's own claim that Option<Id> occupies four bytes rather than sixteen. 366 tests pass, clippy clean under nursery and pedantic."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-07-30T23:56:15.170788734Z
